! Surfaces: the areas of the polygons reproduce the xlsx areas of raw_data columns F, J and K.
! Vertex formulas of the BuildingSurface:Detailed objects: the coordinates are relative to the origin of the zone of the surface (the Zone objects give the origins), X to the east, Y to the north, Z up. Every coordinate is a length in feet x 0.3048 m/ft x k with k = 0.9999620 (fitted: it makes 4 of the 5 distinct non-zero wall coordinates a whole number of feet within 0.5 mm) (k is not a quantity of the prototype IDF, which has only the coordinates in metres: k is a factor fitted here to describe them) (check: with this k the horizontal area of each of the 27 zones agrees with the xlsx area of raw_data column F to within 0.0008 percent, mean 0.0008 percent; with k = 1 the largest difference would be 0.0068 percent); coordinates that are not a whole number of feet are written as feet with 4 decimals and marked (position). NREL PDF Table 13 (Midrise Apartment: 33,740 ft2, 4 floors, aspect ratio 2.7, floor-to-floor height 10 ft) gives a floor plate of 33,740 / 4 = 8,435 ft2 and W = sqrt(plate x aspect ratio) = 150.9 ft, D = W / aspect ratio = 55.9 ft; for comparison the exterior walls of the IDF span X = 0.00 to 151.99 ft, Y = 0.00 to 55.50 ft, Z = 0.00 to 40.00 ft (zone origin + coordinate). The prototype generator and the origin offsets are not in the documents.
